{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/portainer/portainer-ce","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:03:17.343Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/portainer/portainer-ce/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/portainer/portainer-ce"},"readme":"**Portainer Community Edition (CE)** is a lightweight platform that effortlessly delivers containerized applications. It provides seamless management of Docker, Swarm, Kubernetes, and ACI environments. With its intuitive interface and expansive API, Portainer CE empowers you to efficiently manage all your orchestrator resources, including containers, images, volumes, and networks. Effortlessly deploy and efficiently manage containers with the feature-rich toolkit and sleek graphical user interface.\n\n**Portainer Community Edition (CE)** consists of a single container that can run on any cluster. It can be deployed as a Linux container or a Windows native container.\n\n**Portainer Business Edition (BE)** builds on the open-source base. It includes a range of advanced features, including RBAC, Registry Management, Industrial IoT and Edge capabilities that are specific to the needs of business and enterprise users. **Portainer BE** is trusted by customers across various industries, including financial services, information technology, manufacturing, energy, automotive, and healthcare, to simplify the adoption of containers securely with exceptional speed.\n\n- [Compare Portainer CE and Compare Portainer BE](https://portainer.io/products)\n- [3 Nodes Free – Leverage BE on 3 Nodes for as long as you want](https://www.portainer.io/take-3)\n- [Get Started Today](https://www.portainer.io/get-started)\n- [Install Portainer](https://www.portainer.io/install)\n\n## Getting started with Portainer CE\n\n- [Deploy Portainer](https://docs.portainer.io/start/install-ce)\n- [Documentation](https://docs.portainer.io)\n\n## NOTES\n\nIF YOU ARE RUNNING A \"HISTORIC\" VERSION OF PORTAINER (IE OLDER AND 1.23.X) PLEASE EITHER FIRST UPGRADE TO 1.24.1 AND/OR BACKUP YOUR PORTAINER.DB FILE BEFORE ATTEMPTING TO UPGRADE TO CE 2.0; THERE ARE REPORTED ISSUES OF DB CORRUPTION WHEN ATTEMPTING TO UPGRADE FROM SUCH AN OLD VERSION TO THE LATEST IN ONE STEP.\n\n## Getting help\n\nFor Community Edition support:\n* Issues: https://github.com/portainer/portainer/issues\n* FAQ: https://documentation.portainer.io\n* Slack: https://join.slack.com/t/portainer/shared_invite/zt-txh3ljab-52QHTyjCqbe5RibC2lcjKA\n\n## Reporting bugs and contributing\n\n* Want to report a bug or request a feature? Please open [an issue](https://github.com/portainer/portainer/issues/new).","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"portainer","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/portainer","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2020-08-27T05:42:34.203113Z","updated":"2026-09-18T04:37:05.640347Z","categories":["Networking","Integration & delivery","Monitoring & observability"],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":1550304163,"stars":2688},"mediaTypes":["application/vnd.docker.container.image.v1+json","application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json"],"contentTypes":["image"],"storage":110589516356,"tags":[{"name":"alpine-sts","digest":"sha256:4d9a99f4495c005388842b94d72377d5239eac8686543428c3ff7c9b6c0882bb","pushed":"2026-09-18T04:37:04.393531Z","size":48562278,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/arm64","linux/arm/v7","unknown/unknown"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"sts","digest":"sha256:4d616db18cfeb5dd41a69c0958bc825c84483ea9cde1106eb82a5d26f3bd8b0e","pushed":"2026-09-18T04:37:01.914093Z","size":44820755,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/arm64","linux/arm/v7","unknown/unknown","windows/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"alpine","digest":"sha256:4d9a99f4495c005388842b94d72377d5239eac86865